<p class="mb-2">
  Some consumers reports were rejected because they do not have the structure the Web UI needs.
</p>

<p class="mb-4">
  Rejected reports are not materialized, so the data of the processes that sent them is missing or outdated in the Web UI. This can happen when a process reports with a custom or incomplete tracking implementation.
</p>

<div class="data-table-wrapper mb-0">
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Process</th>
        <th>Offset</th>
        <th>Errors</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% details[:rejected].each do |rejection| %>
        <tr>
          <td><%= rejection[:process_id] || 'unknown' %></td>
          <td><%= rejection[:offset] %></td>
          <td>
            <% rejection[:errors].each do |key, message| %>
              <code><%= key %></code> <%= message %><br>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
